pr_info("page at %px\n", addr);

__free_pages(p, 0);                /* return to buddy */
```

The `gfp_t` flags encode context: `GFP_KERNEL` may sleep and reclaim; `GFP_ATOMIC` may not; `__GFP_HIGHMEM` allows highmem; `__GFP_NOWARN` suppresses allocation-failure warnings. The **per-CPU page (PCP) lists** cache batches of order-0 pages to avoid zone-lock contention on the hot path.

Zones (`ZONE_DMA`, `ZONE_DMA32`, `ZONE_NORMAL`, `ZONE_MOVABLE`) partition physical address space by hardware constraints. Each zone has watermarks (`min`, `low`, `high`) that trigger `kswapd` reclaim when free pages dip below thresholds.

